    "tran": "Gamaliēl",
    "phon": "gam-al-ee-ale'",
    "thad": "Gamaliel = \"my recompenser is God\"\n\n1.  a Pharisee and celebrated doctor of the law, who gave prudent\n    worldly advice in the Sanhedrin respecting the treatment of the\n    followers of Jesus of Nazareth. Act 5:34 ff. (A.D.29.) We learn from\n    Act 22:3 that he was the preceptor of Paul. He is generally\n    identified with the very celebrated Jewish doctor Gamaliel, grandson\n    of Hillel, and who is referred to as authority in the Jewish Mishna.",
    "orin": "of Hebrew origin H1583]",
    "tdnt": "None",
