  "G5351": {
    "orig": "φθείρω",
    "tran": "phtheirō",
    "phon": "fthi'-ro",
    "thad": "1.  to corrupt, to destroy\n    a.  in the opinion of the Jews, the temple was corrupted or\n        \"destroyed\" when anyone defiled or in the slightest degree\n        damaged anything in it, or if its guardians neglected their\n        duties\n    b.  to lead away a Christian church from that state of knowledge and\n        holiness in which it ought to abide\n    c.  to be destroyed, to perish\n    d.  in an ethical sense, to corrupt, deprave",
    "orin": "probably strengthened from phthio (to pine or waste)",
    "tdnt": "10:33,1",
    "posp": "Verb",
    "sdef": "Probably strengthened from φθίω phthiō (to pine or\nwaste): properly to shrivel or wither, that is, to spoil (by any\nprocess) or (genitive) to ruin (especially figuratively by moral\ninfluences, to deprave): - corrupt (self), defile, destroy.",
    "atra": "fqeirw",
    "shor": "To corrupt, to destroy"
  },
