    "thad": "Philip = \"lover of horses\"\n\n1.  an apostle of Christ\n2.  an evangelist and one of the seven deacons of the Jerusalem church\n3.  tetrarch of Trachonitis, was brother to Herod Antipas, by the\n    father's, but not by the mother's side. Philip was born of\n    Cleopatra, of Jerusalem, and Herod of Malthace, a Samaritan: he died\n    in the twentieth year of Tiberias, five years after his mention in\n    Luk 3:1. He built Caesarea Philippi. His step brother Herod Antipas,\n    married his wife unlawfully. (Gill)\n4.  see G2542, Caesarea Philippi",
    "orin": "from G5384 and G2462",
    "tdnt": "None",
